From: "D.R.racer" <drracer@seznam.cz>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 12:08:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: cedrus: h264 encoder: number the buffers of both
 queues

The encoder left v4l2_buffer.sequence at 0 on both queues, which
v4l2-compliance -s reports as five streaming failures. Number every job:
the picture (OUTPUT) and coded (CAPTURE) buffers of a job get the same
value, counted from 0 at each stream start. A failed job consumes a
number, so userspace sees gaps as lost frames; the empty last buffer of
a drain carries none.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_enc_h264.c | 4 ++++
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_enc_h264.h | 6 ++++++
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_enc_h264.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_enc_h264.c
index 6da67fd7d..ec9eac5a0 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_enc_h264.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_enc_h264.c
@@ -622,6 +622,7 @@ static int cedrus_enc_h264_setup(struct cedrus_context *cedrus_ctx)
 	/* Everything the error path frees must be valid from here on. */
 	h264_ctx->deblk = NULL;
 	h264_ctx->mv = NULL;
+	h264_ctx->sequence = 0;
 	memset(h264_ctx->refs, 0, sizeof(h264_ctx->refs));
 
 	/* Macroblock Information Buffer */
@@ -1604,6 +1605,9 @@ static int cedrus_enc_h264_job_finish(struct cedrus_context *ctx, int state)
 				     size, h264_ctx->overflow_qp_bump);
 	}
 
+	ctx->job.buffer_picture->sequence = h264_ctx->sequence;
+	v4l2_buffer->sequence = h264_ctx->sequence++;
+
 	if (state != VB2_BUF_STATE_DONE) {
 		/*
 		 * The reconstruction of this job is unusable and the decoder
diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_enc_h264.h b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_enc_h264.h
index 6ca119748..f0ebdb062 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_enc_h264.h
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_enc_h264.h
@@ -113,6 +113,12 @@ struct cedrus_enc_h264_context {
 	dma_addr_t			mv_dma;
 	unsigned int			mv_size;
 
+	/*
+	 * Job counter, reported as v4l2_buffer.sequence on both queues. Failed
+	 * jobs consume a number too.
+	 */
+	u32				sequence;
+
 	/*
